{"id": "live-375", "title": "Torchlight Sues Prime Group to Halt JW Marriott Chicago Conversion Work", "category": "lending-foreclosure", "status": "filed", "date": "2026-10-30", "jurisdiction": "Circuit Court of Cook County, Illinois, Chancery Division", "state": "IL", "amount": "Injunctive relief sought; no damages figure stated", "source": "live", "source_url": "https://therealdeal.com/chicago/2026/11/04/torchlight-sues-reschkes-firm-to-stop-loop-conversion/", "summary": "Torchlight Loan Services, the special servicer that foreclosed on the JW Marriott Chicago hotel on behalf of CMBS bondholders, sued developer Mike Reschke's Prime Group in Cook County Circuit Court on October 30, 2026. The complaint alleges Prime Group proceeded with demolition and conversion work on office floors in the same historic LaSalle Street building without the hotel's consent, and that the work cut off the hotel's phone and internet service during a sold-out stretch. Torchlight is asking the court to halt the conversion work until Prime Group secures the hotel's consent.", "significance": "The suit tests how far a CMBS special servicer can go to protect an operating hotel asset from disruption by a co-owner's redevelopment next door, a fact pattern increasingly common as Chicago's LaSalle Street Reimagined program converts distressed office towers to housing above and alongside hotels and other operating tenants. For lenders, servicers and developers sharing a single historic building under converted uses, the case previews the consent and operational-disruption disputes likely to recur as more office-to-residential conversions proceed next to live commercial operations.", "judge": null, "tags": ["cmbs", "chicago", "hotel-conversion", "special-servicer", "lasalle-street"]}
